      "body": "`PrecompileReader.suppliedBalance()` reads HyperCore precompile `0x811` and treats it as if it were a supplied-balance-only source:\n\n```solidity\n(,,, supplied) = abi.decode(res, (uint64, uint64, uint64, uint64));\n```\n\nThat keeps only the fourth decoded word. The 0x811 user state is a borrow/lend user token state, not a pure supply balance. Its layout is:\n\n```text\nborrow.basis, borrow.value, supply.basis, supply.value\n```\n\nSo Monetrix books the asset side, `supply.value`, but drops the liability side, `borrow.value`.\n\n`MonetrixAccountant.totalBackingSigned()` calls `_readL1Backing()` for the Vault and multisig L1 accounts. For each registered supplied slot, `_readL1Backing()` adds either `PrecompileReader.suppliedUsdcEvm(account)` or `PrecompileReader.suppliedNotionalUsdcFromPerp(...)` to backing. There is no matching read of `borrow.value`, no netting, and no check that the account has zero 0x811 borrow liability.\n\nThe inflated value feeds directly into the settlement gate:\n\n```text\ntotalBackingSigned() -> surplus() -> distributableSurplus() -> settleDailyPnL()\n```\n\nGate 3 in `settleDailyPnL()` requires `proposedYield <= distributableSurplus()`. That gate is supposed to keep Operator-submitted yield within real surplus. Here the bound itself is wrong because it is computed from gross 0x811 supply while ignoring 0x811 borrow debt.\n\nThis is not an Operator-compromise or arbitrary-destination issue. The Operator only calls the normal, code-bounded `settle()` and `distributeYield()` pipeline. The submitted yield is accepted by the protocol's own on-chain `distributableSurplus()` and APR cap. The bug is that the Accountant's on-chain safety bound overstates backing.\n\nThis is also in the audit's stated area of concern. The README explicitly calls out the Accountant 4-gate settle pipeline, vectors that over-report `totalBackingSigned()`, and HyperCore precompile read semantics. The affected files are in scope: `src/core/PrecompileReader.sol`, `src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol`, and `src/core/MonetrixVault.sol`.\n\n### Impact\n\nWhen an L1 account has a counted 0x811 supply position and a 0x811 borrow liability, Monetrix can overstate USDM backing by the ignored borrow amount.\n\nIf the real net backing has no surplus, but `totalBackingSigned()` reports surplus because it counted gross supply, `settle()` can move principal USDC from the Vault to `YieldEscrow` as if it were yield. `distributeYield()` then finalizes the damage:\n\n- the user share is minted as USDM and injected into sUSDM;\n- the insurance share is deposited into `InsuranceFund`;\n- the foundation share is transferred out as USDC.\n\nThe PoC demonstrates a 10,000 USDC unsupported yield distribution. After distribution, sUSDM assets increased, while USDM is underbacked by the same 10,000 USDC amount.\n\nMedium severity is appropriate. The impact is real solvency damage, not rounding dust and not a display-only error. It is still bounded by normal settlement conditions, EVM USDC liquidity, the APR cap, and the need for a PM/BLP borrow liability to exist, so this is not a High-severity immediate drain.\n\n### Why the same-token PoC is used\n\nThe PoC uses the same-token borrow/supply state as the minimal direct reproduction because it is exactly the four-word tuple decoded by `suppliedBalance()`. This directly shows that the contract reads `supply.value` while dropping the decoded `borrow.value`.\n\nThe root issue is broader than the same-token case: the settlement accounting has no path that subtracts 0x811 borrow liabilities for the account before treating 0x811 supply as USDM backing. In a cross-token PM state, the Accountant would also need to query and value borrowed-token liabilities, not only registered supplied-token assets.\n\n### Recommended mitigation\n\nDecode the full 0x811 borrow/lend user state instead of exposing only `supply.value`. For every 0x811 supplied position counted as backing, subtract the corresponding `borrow.value` after valuing it in USDC terms. If the PM account can borrow tokens outside the registered supplied-token list, those borrowable token liabilities must also be queried and subtracted. As a conservative fallback, settlement should revert while any nonzero 0x811 borrow liability is not modeled by the Accountant.",
      "proofOfConcept": "The Monetrix README requires High/Medium submissions to use the provided template at `test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol`, edit it in place, and write the exploit inside `test_submissionValidity`. This PoC follows that requirement: it only replaces the placeholder body of `test_submissionValidity`; it does not rename the test, does not create a new file, and does not modify `setUp()`.\n\nReplace `test_submissionValidity()` with the function below:\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_submissionValidity() public {\n    uint256 principal = 1_000_000e6;\n    uint256 retainedEvmUsdc = 200_000e6;\n    uint256 grossSuppliedUsdc = 900_000e6;\n    uint256 ignoredBorrowDebt = 100_000e6;\n    uint256 unsupportedYield = 10_000e6;\n\n    _deposit(user1, principal);\n    _stake(user1, 100_000e6);\n\n    vm.prank(admin);\n    vault.setBridgeRetentionAmount(retainedEvmUsdc);\n\n    vm.warp(block.timestamp + config.bridgeInterval());\n    vm.prank(operator);\n    vault.keeperBridge(MonetrixVault.BridgeTarget.Vault);\n    assertEq(usdc.balanceOf(address(vault)), retainedEvmUsdc, \"cash retained for yield/redemptions\");\n\n    uint64 suppliedL1 = uint64(grossSuppliedUsdc * 100);\n    uint64 borrowL1 = uint64(ignoredBorrowDebt * 100);\n\n    vm.prank(operator);\n    vault.supplyToBlp(uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX), suppliedL1);\n\n    _PoCMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE)).setResponse(\n        abi.encode(address(vault), uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)),\n        abi.encode(borrowL1, borrowL1, suppliedL1, suppliedL1)\n    );\n\n    uint256 netL1Backing = grossSuppliedUsdc - ignoredBorrowDebt;\n    uint256 trueBackingBefore = retainedEvmUsdc + netL1Backing;\n    uint256 reportedBackingBefore = uint256(accountant.totalBackingSigned());\n\n    assertEq(trueBackingBefore, usdm.totalSupply(), \"net backing has no surplus\");\n    assertEq(\n        reportedBackingBefore,\n        retainedEvmUsdc + grossSuppliedUsdc,\n        \"Accountant counts gross supplied value\"\n    );\n    assertEq(\n        reportedBackingBefore - trueBackingBefore,\n        ignoredBorrowDebt,\n        \"borrow side of 0x811 is ignored\"\n    );\n\n    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 365 days);\n\n    uint256 susdmAssetsBefore = susdm.totalAssets();\n\n    vm.prank(operator);\n    vault.settle(unsupportedYield);\n\n    vm.prank(operator);\n    vault.distributeYield();\n\n    uint256 userShare = (unsupportedYield * config.userYieldBps()) / 10_000;\n    uint256 trueBackingAfter =\n        usdc.balanceOf(address(vault)) + usdc.balanceOf(address(redeemEscrow)) + netL1Backing;\n\n    assertEq(susdm.totalAssets(), susdmAssetsBefore + userShare, \"unsupported yield was injected\");\n    assertEq(usdm.totalSupply() - trueBackingAfter, unsupportedYield, \"USDM became underbacked\");\n}\n```\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nforge test --match-path test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol -vvv\n```\n\nExpected result:\n\n```text\n[PASS] test_submissionValidity()\n```\n\nThe test creates 1,000,000 USDM of liabilities, keeps 200,000 USDC on EVM, registers a USDC 0x811 supplied slot, and mocks 0x811 as 900,000 USDC supplied with 100,000 USDC borrowed. Net backing has no real surplus:\n\n```text\n200,000 EVM USDC + 900,000 supplied - 100,000 borrow = 1,000,000 USDC\n```\n\nBut the Accountant ignores the borrow side and reports:\n\n```text\n200,000 EVM USDC + 900,000 supplied = 1,100,000 USDC\n```\n\nThe Operator then calls the normal `settle()` and `distributeYield()` path with `unsupportedYield = 10,000 USDC`. The call succeeds because Gate 3 sees the inflated `distributableSurplus()`. The final assertions prove that unsupported yield was injected into sUSDM and USDM became underbacked by 10,000 USDC.",
      "linesOfCode": "https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/PrecompileReader.sol#L84-L90,https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/PrecompileReader.sol#L132-L161,https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol#L117-L156,https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol#L180-L191,https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol#L213-L221,https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixVault.sol#L364-L414",
